llenge-01", "project": "proj-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "By integrating the governance module's immutability as a fixed constraint, WAKE identifies its own boundary conditions as testable assumptions. Governance stability is maintained through the verifiable rejection of model-authored proposal transitions.", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "notebook-f1c16003-obedience-failure", "project": "proj-obedience-failure-01", "provenance": ["source-f1c16003c47b4e8f", "source-b1a16f9e7285493e", "source-cbeddd6778fc48b1"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Synthesizing multiple source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Accountability is enforced via strict bifurcation of inquiry (model-driven) and governance (state-committed). This design prevents models from subverting the research record by ensuring that only valid, rule-compliant transitions are committed to durable history.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "79a56f17690e50566343518403e239d78fb6bd10b7cd03952495707f208f89a2", "hash": "9772cd69a0f3b45579a0212ac37ffe7ec1585277c1df03e84aa4323b370320ea"}, {"seq": 2426, "time": "2026-10-28T15:36:52.684628+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 47453, "provider_input_hash": "7dacb5fa159c8db020c403c6dd03efb79096734373792e4d00c71fdfbda880bb", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "w-df8bdc5303e04d00"}, "prev_hash": "9772cd69a0f3b45579a0212ac37ffe7ec1585277c1df03e84aa4323b370320ea", "hash": "53df7fad09503455248c10fcb9b978eba5bc7a92f9149730c9267376268a3ce8"}, {"seq": 2427, "time": "2026-10-28T15:37:36.620659+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_finished", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_call_made": false, "provider_input_chars": 47453, "provider_input_hash": "7dacb5fa159c8db020c403c6dd03efb79096734373792e4d00c71fdfbda880bb", "result": "daily_quota", "retry_after_seconds": 55047.85650873184}, "id": "w-df8bdc5303e04d00"}, "prev_hash": "53df7fad09503455248c10fcb9b978eba5bc7a92f9149730c9267376268a3ce8", "hash": "5e4b392b326f1802b15d95bcc750d7dfd70bc8f4a5bb7b8c9e7f50ff1ac9b716"}, {"seq": 2428, "time": "2026-10-28T15:38:21.429851+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 47453, "provider_input_hash": "7dacb5fa159c8db020c403c6dd03efb79096734373792e4d00c71fdfbda880bb", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "w-df8bdc5303e04d00"}, "prev_hash": "5e4b392b326f1802b15d95bcc750d7dfd70bc8f4a5bb7b8c9e7f50ff1ac9b716", "hash": "c303638ec786b1e5fba1fc935addba830736876b79de4b5aecd8ce610ff75f79"}, {"